VEN`, matching the docstring, the test, and FIN-212.\n\nCI: run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n**The fix:** `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That makes `2.665` round to `2.66` as the test expects, and `2.675` still rounds to `2.68`. Nothing else changed.\n\n**CI:**\n- The first run (ci-0001) passed.\n- The PR couldn't be opened at first because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into it and re-ran CI on the updated branch, since the code had changed. That run (ci-0002, commit `0a9452f727`) also passed.\n\n**PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check what it actually says. I went by the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nI didn't merge the PR: policy requires a code owner to approve before anything is merged into main.", "type": "text"}]}]}